# What the language bar should say
#
# MikroDash is a Go binary serving a TypeScript frontend.
#
# This file used to explain away 4.1 MB of JavaScript: a 136-gate verification
# harness that compared the app against a frozen recording of the Node
# implementation it replaced. That harness was retired on 2026-09-01 -- the checks
# worth keeping became Go tests in `internal/verify/` and TypeScript tests in
# `web/test/` -- so there is very little left to explain.
#
# What remains is 15 tracked .js files, 136 KB in total:
#
#   tools/        capture and generation utilities. `capture-fixtures.js` reads a
#                 live router, `make-golden.js` builds the collector goldens Go
#                 tests replay, and the `*-ts.js` transforms regenerate
#                 `web/src/gen/` from committed tables.
#   web/test/     the frontend's own tests, plus the runner. JavaScript-hosted
#                 because testing TypeScript needs a JavaScript runtime.
#   vendor        chart.umd.min.js, third-party, self-hosted because this project
#                 serves no CDN assets.
#
# The runtime image contains no node or npm binary and no JavaScript except the
# compiled frontend bundle, which is built from TypeScript.
#
# NOTE THIS IS PRESENTATION, NOT REMOVAL. Everything below is still in the tree,
# still maintained, and still runs.

# ── The verification harness ──────────────────────────────────────────────
tools/**            linguist-vendored

# ── Genuinely third-party, vendored to avoid a CDN ────────────────────────
web/public/vendor/** linguist-vendored

# ── Recordings and build output, not hand-written source ──────────────────
#
# `internal/resource/testdata/live-resources.js` is a frozen oracle a Go test
# replays; `web/dist/` is build output.
testdata/**         linguist-generated
internal/*/testdata/** linguist-generated
web/dist/**         linguist-generated
